   "text": "I read the macrocycle region by region and wrote it as one SMILES, with the stereocentres assigned from the wedges and hashes.\n\n**Ring path.** I traced the ring clockwise from the N-methyl-leucine. The units, in order, are:\n1. N-methyl-Leu (isobutyl side chain) joined to the N-methyl amide on the CH2\u2013CH=CH\u2013C(=O)\u2013O linker.\n2. The ester O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2\u2013C(=O)\u2013C(=O) connecting to the piperidine nitrogen.\n3. The pipecolic acid, whose carboxyl forms an ester with the benzylic CH(O).\n4. That benzylic CH, which carries the CH2CH2-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl) arm and a meta-phenylene ring.\n5. The meta-phenylene NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)\u2013NH succinamide bridge, leading to phenylglycine.\n6. The 3-acetamidophenylalanine unit.\n7. The proline, whose carbonyl closes the ring onto the N-methyl-Leu nitrogen.\n\n**Alkene.** The CH=CH bond is drawn wavy, so I gave it no cis/trans label.\n\n**Stereocentres.** I assigned each from the drawn wedge or hash using CIP priorities and then converted to @/@@ with the SMILES neighbour order:\n- Leu \u03b1-carbon: S\n- Pipecolic \u03b1-carbon: S\n- Benzylic CH\u2013O: R\n- Phenylglycine \u03b1-carbon: S\n- Phenylalanine \u03b1-carbon: S\n- Proline \u03b1-carbon: R\n\nSMILES: CC(C)C[C@H]1C(=O)N(C)CC=CC(=O)OCC(C)(C)C(=O)C(=O)N2CCCC[C@H]2C(=O)O[C@H](CCc2ccc(OC)c(OC)c2)c2cccc(c2)NC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@@H](c2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccc(NC(C)=O)c2)C(=O)N2CCC[C@@H]2C(=O)N1C"
